{
  "about": [
    "The session token a request carries, by its headers ([name, value] pairs, in order).",
    "One table for both sides of the bridge/gateway contract: the gateway reads it in",
    "middleware/auth.rs (session_token_from_headers, through bearer_credential and",
    "cookie_pair) and the bridge in tests/bridge/test_session_token_parity.py",
    "(dependencies._extract_session_token).",
    "Rules: the sources are read in order, Authorization: Bearer, then X-Session-Token,",
    "then the session_token cookie, and an empty one is skipped. The auth scheme is",
    "case-insensitive (RFC 9110 section 11.1), so bearer, BEARER and BeArEr are Bearer;",
    "one space must follow it (a tab or nothing does not make it a bearer credential);",
    "the token is what follows, with surrounding whitespace removed. A cookie's name is",
    "what precedes its first '=', with surrounding whitespace removed (session_token =x",
    "is the session cookie), and is case-sensitive; its value is what follows, trimmed.",
    "A repeated header is read by its first value.",
    "'token' null: the request carries no session token.",
    "Not in the table, as the two read them differently: a repeated session_token cookie",
    "(the gateway takes the first one with a value, the bridge the last one) and a quoted",
    "cookie value (the bridge unquotes it). Behind the gateway neither reaches the bridge:",
    "the proxy forwards no session_token cookie.",
    "Both sides also refuse to run with fewer cases than this table has now (59):",
    "add cases freely, and raise that floor in both tests when you do."
  ],
